From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix EDMA resource lifecycle

Allocate EDMA error statistics before enabling interrupts. Keep them alive
until IRQ teardown. Track every successful IRQ request and enabled clock so
partial setup failures and driver removal release only live resources.

Preserve signed IRQ lookup errors and validate child nodes and reset
operations. Centralize ring and hardware cleanup. Also disable the selected
per-port TX rings instead of accidentally disabling the first CPU rings.

Track enabled NAPI separately from registration and quiesce shared RX before
unregistering ports and freeing statistics. Unmap queued RX buffers using
the original mapping type and size, free partial assembly, and bound partial
ring allocation unwind with a signed index.

Respect napi_complete_done() before rearming and serialize completion, IRQ
scheduling and interrupt enable/disable under a per-ring lock. Stop cannot
be undone by the polling tail.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
